hine like yourself. Book jacket.\n\n### Bibliographic information\n\nTitle  | The Age of AI: And Our Human Future\nAuthors  | Henry Kissinger, Eric Schmidt, Daniel P. Huttenlocher\nEdition  | illustrated\nPublisher  | Little, Brown, 2021\nISBN  | 0316273805, 9780316273800\nLength  | 254 pages\nSubjects  | Computers › Artificial Intelligence › General\nComputers / Artificial Intelligence / General\nPolitical Science / Public Policy / Science & Technology Policy\nSocial Science / Technology Studies\n   |  \nExport Citation  | BiBTeX EndNote RefMan--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTechnology and the Character of Contemporary Life: A Philosophical Inquiry - Albert Borgmann - Google Books (https://books.google.com/books/about/Technology_and_the_Character_of_Contempo.html?id=-JNj1R9RNqoC)\nciteturn353search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 42.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n### References to this book\n\n | The Absent Body\nDrew Leder\nLimited preview - 1990\n | \n\n | The Malaise of Modernity\nCharles Taylor\nNo preview available - 1991\n | \n\nAll Book Search results &raquo;\n\n### About the author (1984)\n\nAlbert Borgmann (1937-2023) was Regents Professor of Philosophy at the University of Montana. He is the author of Technology and the Character of Contemporary Life, Crossing the Postmodern Divide, and Holding On to Reality: The Nature of Information at the Turn of the Millennium, all published by the University of Chicago Press.\n\n### Bibliographic information\n\nTitle  | Technology and the Character of Contemporary Life: A Philosophical Inquiry\nAuthor  | Albert Borgmann\nEdition  | revised\nPublisher  | University of Chicago Press, 1984\nISBN  | 0226066290, 9780226066295\nLength  | 302 pages\nSubjects  | Family & Relationships › General\nFamily & Relationships / General\nPhilosophy / General\nScience / Philosophy & Social Aspects\nSocial Science / General\nTechnology & Engineering / Social Aspects-----------------